WEBVTT

00:01:38.410 --> 00:01:39.770
Quiet!

00:01:44.380 --> 00:01:46.400
Keep it down, Yotsuya!

00:01:46.650 --> 00:01:48.550
You made so much noise
last night!

00:01:52.750 --> 00:01:54.140
Cut it out!

00:01:55.720 --> 00:01:56.880
Get up already!

00:01:57.960 --> 00:01:59.010
Grandma...!

00:02:01.730 --> 00:02:02.420
When'd you come in?!

00:02:02.600 --> 00:02:04.620
You were supposed
to pick me up!

00:02:06.030 --> 00:02:06.820
Was it today?

00:02:07.570 --> 00:02:08.830
Knucklehead!

00:02:18.010 --> 00:02:21.500
Manager, what do you
think of my Yusaku?

00:02:28.720 --> 00:02:29.810
Why do you ask?

00:02:30.490 --> 00:02:32.510
Isn't he a bit hopeless?

00:02:32.630 --> 00:02:33.820
Well, yes...

00:02:37.130 --> 00:02:39.960
But...
He's very sweet!

00:02:40.870 --> 00:02:42.490
He's considerate.

00:02:43.140 --> 00:02:46.070
And popular with my niece
and his girlfriend.

00:02:46.740 --> 00:02:48.030
He has a girlfriend?

00:02:48.880 --> 00:02:50.710
Yes, her name is
Kozue Nanao.

00:03:10.030 --> 00:03:11.930
So you're Godai's
grandmother?

00:03:16.540 --> 00:03:19.000
Pleased to meet you.
I'm Kozue Nanao.

00:03:19.370 --> 00:03:22.060
She seems like a nice
girl, Yusaku.

00:03:22.140 --> 00:03:24.900
Here, Kozue. The book
you asked me for.

00:03:24.980 --> 00:03:26.370
Thanks!

00:03:26.750 --> 00:03:28.910
This book's very technical...

00:03:28.980 --> 00:03:31.070
and expensive, so I was
reluctant to buy it.

00:03:31.350 --> 00:03:33.680
But I need it to
do a report.

00:03:34.550 --> 00:03:36.780
I knew you'd come
through, Godai!

00:03:37.320 --> 00:03:39.040
You're studying hard.

00:03:39.130 --> 00:03:41.250
I was lucky to find it.

00:03:41.530 --> 00:03:44.590
Liar! You bought it
on the way here.

00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:45.630
Grandma!

00:03:48.800 --> 00:03:53.790
He's always trying to look
good in front of the ladies.

00:03:56.280 --> 00:04:00.140
Thank you, Godai. I know you
looked for it just for me.

00:04:00.750 --> 00:04:01.730
I really appreciate it!

00:04:01.850 --> 00:04:02.680
Don't mention it...

00:04:13.590 --> 00:04:16.780
Forgive me, Kozue, for bringing
her along without telling you.

00:04:16.860 --> 00:04:17.550
Not at all!

00:04:17.630 --> 00:04:21.490
I was happy you introduced me
to a member of your family.

00:04:22.940 --> 00:04:24.630
It isn't anything like that!

00:04:24.840 --> 00:04:26.530
Would you marry him?

00:04:26.970 --> 00:04:27.800
May I?

00:04:28.280 --> 00:04:30.470
Grandma! There you
go again!

00:04:30.740 --> 00:04:35.070
You don't want to?
Is there someone else?

00:04:44.620 --> 00:04:46.010
I never said
I didn't want to.

00:04:47.790 --> 00:04:50.850
He's so indecisive...
Look at him blush.

00:04:51.570 --> 00:04:54.300
I'll massage your shoulders
every single day, Grandma!

00:04:54.470 --> 00:04:55.490
Thank you.

00:04:55.700 --> 00:04:58.720
I only hope I live long enough
to see Yusaku's wedding day.

00:04:58.810 --> 00:04:59.970
Of course you will!

00:05:11.220 --> 00:05:12.580
Welcome back.

00:05:13.950 --> 00:05:14.640
Hi.

00:05:14.750 --> 00:05:15.770
We're back.

00:05:16.290 --> 00:05:18.340
Did you go somewhere
together?

00:05:18.730 --> 00:05:19.590
Well, sort of...

00:05:19.860 --> 00:05:21.620
We went to see Kozue.

00:05:21.860 --> 00:05:22.620
Grandma!

00:05:23.460 --> 00:05:24.250
How did it go?

00:05:24.360 --> 00:05:26.350
Such a sweet girl!

00:05:26.630 --> 00:05:28.390
She'd make Yusaku
a great wife.

00:05:28.470 --> 00:05:31.200
Grandma, the manager has
better things to do!

00:05:33.040 --> 00:05:36.100
He's upset because I
spoiled their date.

00:05:36.180 --> 00:05:36.900
Stop that!

00:05:37.210 --> 00:05:38.870
Why didn't you kiss her?

00:05:40.610 --> 00:05:41.440
Quiet!

00:05:50.620 --> 00:05:51.270
Fess up!

00:05:51.460 --> 00:05:52.110
About what?

00:05:52.660 --> 00:05:56.890
Who do you like better?
Kozue or the manager?

00:05:57.130 --> 00:05:58.650
Not now!

00:05:58.800 --> 00:05:59.590
Decide!

00:05:59.900 --> 00:06:00.380
Why?

00:06:00.470 --> 00:06:02.960
You can't marry both
at once.

00:06:03.470 --> 00:06:06.160
I'm still a student!

00:06:06.410 --> 00:06:09.200
Big deal! If you fall in
love, get married.

00:06:09.640 --> 00:06:10.900
Why does it have to
be that way?

00:06:10.980 --> 00:06:12.410
That's what it is
to be a man!

00:06:12.480 --> 00:06:15.970
Let grandma help you
choose a wife!

00:06:18.020 --> 00:06:19.950
You keep out of this!

00:06:21.020 --> 00:06:23.920
Hurry up and decide.
Now's your chance.

00:06:24.520 --> 00:06:27.040
He can't make up his
mind by himself.

00:06:28.430 --> 00:06:29.890
Now just a damn minute!

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:31.520
Sounds interesting...

00:06:36.440 --> 00:06:40.370
Personally, I think Kozue
is the safer choice.

00:06:40.610 --> 00:06:42.660
She's got no sex appeal.

00:06:42.840 --> 00:06:43.670
That'll come.

00:06:43.810 --> 00:06:46.300
Sit down, everybody!

00:06:47.180 --> 00:06:49.610
Let's discuss it over
some sake.

00:06:49.750 --> 00:06:50.840
Sounds good.

00:06:51.050 --> 00:06:53.950
I like it! Don't mind
if I do.

00:06:54.350 --> 00:06:56.140
We don't have glasses.

00:06:56.220 --> 00:06:58.340
The glasses are over there...

00:06:58.430 --> 00:07:00.450
I'll get them, Grandma.

00:07:00.590 --> 00:07:03.850
We'll decide right now!
There's nothing to fear!

00:07:41.070 --> 00:07:43.260
Yusaku, choose the one
you like better.

00:07:44.170 --> 00:07:47.690
But not both at once.
You'll get a tummy ache.

00:07:51.950 --> 00:07:54.610
Let me see...

00:07:56.150 --> 00:08:01.880
lce Cream

00:08:16.070 --> 00:08:17.050
What happened?

00:08:18.170 --> 00:08:19.530
They all melted!

00:08:26.410 --> 00:08:28.370
You took too long
to decide!

00:08:45.570 --> 00:08:48.730
He hasn't changed a bit...

00:08:49.000 --> 00:08:51.960
He won't be able to choose
a wife by himself.

00:08:59.350 --> 00:09:02.780
Oh well. Guess I'll be
staying here a while.

00:09:10.160 --> 00:09:11.680
She has someone?

00:09:12.060 --> 00:09:13.490
Sure does!

00:09:16.630 --> 00:09:20.250
The manager says he's
just a "friend."

00:09:20.570 --> 00:09:23.630
But he seems quite
serious about her.

00:09:23.800 --> 00:09:25.730
Godai's quite concerned.

00:09:26.210 --> 00:09:27.970
Has Yusaku met him?

00:09:28.040 --> 00:09:29.230
Sees him all the time.

00:09:29.480 --> 00:09:30.700
That fool!

00:09:30.910 --> 00:09:32.630
Would you like to meet
him, grandma?

00:09:32.950 --> 00:09:37.080
Clock Hill Tennis Club

00:09:54.470 --> 00:09:55.990
He's a hunk.

00:09:56.070 --> 00:09:57.400
Didn't I tell you?

00:10:08.150 --> 00:10:09.010
Darn!

00:10:09.880 --> 00:10:12.040
Take ten, everyone!

00:10:16.960 --> 00:10:18.050
Who could that be?

00:10:25.370 --> 00:10:27.490
Do you enjoy tennis,
Grandma?

00:10:27.830 --> 00:10:28.950
It looks fun.

00:10:29.440 --> 00:10:31.160
The two of you make
a fine couple.

00:10:38.540 --> 00:10:40.630
So she's Ms. Otonashi's
acquaintance...

00:10:43.150 --> 00:10:45.170
Her grandmother, maybe?

00:10:52.330 --> 00:10:53.020
How do you do!

00:10:53.260 --> 00:10:54.750
And hi to you, too!

00:11:00.300 --> 00:11:01.260
She seems pretty sharp...

00:11:03.770 --> 00:11:06.460
Thank you for being so
good to my grandchild.

00:11:06.540 --> 00:11:08.470
The pleasure's mine.

00:11:14.050 --> 00:11:17.110
I'd like to get to
know you better.

00:11:17.580 --> 00:11:18.910
You do?

00:11:21.020 --> 00:11:22.950
I'd better take advantage
of this chance...

00:11:23.420 --> 00:11:27.410
You're welcome
to visit any time.

00:11:27.630 --> 00:11:28.590
Do you mind?

00:11:28.730 --> 00:11:29.560
Not at all.

00:11:29.960 --> 00:11:32.520
May I bring my grandchild?

00:11:33.000 --> 00:11:35.760
Of course!
Right, Ms. Otonashi?

00:11:38.810 --> 00:11:40.500
This is your grandmother,
right?

00:11:40.770 --> 00:11:42.390
Godai's grandmother.

00:11:57.690 --> 00:11:59.950
He seems like a nice
man, Manager.

00:12:01.230 --> 00:12:02.060
Didn't I tell you?

00:12:02.200 --> 00:12:05.030
He's always willing
to help the ladies.

00:12:05.370 --> 00:12:08.060
Come pick me up this
coming Saturday.

00:12:08.370 --> 00:12:10.160
But I...

00:12:12.340 --> 00:12:14.630
We're going to Mitaka's
place?! What for?!

00:12:15.610 --> 00:12:17.000
He invited us.

00:12:17.610 --> 00:12:19.630
Why do I have to go
with you?!

00:12:20.010 --> 00:12:22.740
Can't hurt to learn about
your rival in love.

00:12:23.580 --> 00:12:24.940
You're meddling again...

00:12:26.590 --> 00:12:28.550
The manager's going, too.

00:12:29.520 --> 00:12:31.880
Grandma! Are you trying
to embarrass me?!

00:12:32.190 --> 00:12:33.080
What do you mean?

00:12:33.160 --> 00:12:36.320
She'll just see how
much richer he is!

00:12:36.500 --> 00:12:38.960
Good! Maybe that'll
make you give her up.

00:12:39.030 --> 00:12:40.360
Why would I give her up?

00:12:40.770 --> 00:12:43.830
Then let's go. You need
to know where you stand.

00:13:11.740 --> 00:13:12.640
My...!

00:13:25.930 --> 00:13:27.450
Impressive!

00:13:28.730 --> 00:13:29.780
Very...

00:13:33.800 --> 00:13:35.700
What's the matter?

00:13:36.640 --> 00:13:38.300
Please make yourselves
at home.

00:13:38.410 --> 00:13:39.170
Thank you.

00:13:43.080 --> 00:13:44.700
It's very tidy.

00:13:45.250 --> 00:13:48.240
I hire a maid who comes
once a week.

00:13:48.980 --> 00:13:50.240
I'm embarrassed
to admit it, though.

00:13:50.750 --> 00:13:52.740
Are you paying for
everything yourself?

00:13:53.360 --> 00:13:55.050
It's only about 200,OOO yen
per month.

00:13:55.360 --> 00:13:57.620
No wonder there's
no comparison.

00:13:58.060 --> 00:14:00.220
I AM poor, you know!

00:14:00.860 --> 00:14:01.820
Now, now...

00:14:13.640 --> 00:14:16.800
Mind if I look at your
record collection?

00:14:17.150 --> 00:14:17.980
Go right ahead.

00:14:20.150 --> 00:14:21.440
Shall I put something on?

00:14:26.660 --> 00:14:28.850
Are you an opera fan,
Mr. Mitaka?

00:14:30.230 --> 00:14:31.450
Let me see!

00:14:32.660 --> 00:14:34.820
Quite a collection
you've got here.

00:14:35.130 --> 00:14:36.680
Manager, look at this!

00:14:37.530 --> 00:14:40.320
It's the record we
listened to together

00:14:40.400 --> 00:14:41.120
in my room.

00:14:43.840 --> 00:14:46.170
It was a quiet, lovely
moonlit night.

00:14:47.680 --> 00:14:49.770
You were a bit mellow
from your drinks.

00:14:50.280 --> 00:14:51.400
Was I?

00:14:52.620 --> 00:14:54.610
Oh yes, I remember!

00:14:55.020 --> 00:14:56.880
That was hilarious!

00:14:57.150 --> 00:15:00.440
Akemi can't carry a tune
when she's drunk!

00:15:01.520 --> 00:15:02.740
R-right...

00:15:08.330 --> 00:15:11.120
I want to show you something,
Ms. Otonashi.

00:15:11.530 --> 00:15:12.620
Follow me.

00:15:16.110 --> 00:15:17.160
Take a look.

00:15:25.980 --> 00:15:27.000
How cute!

00:15:27.780 --> 00:15:30.770
I collected them during
my tennis travels.

00:15:31.390 --> 00:15:34.320
I had no idea you
were a collector.

00:15:34.620 --> 00:15:37.020
As I began buying them,
the collection grew.

00:15:39.760 --> 00:15:42.280
I bought this one at
a flea market in Naples.

00:15:42.630 --> 00:15:46.820
And I bought this when
I went to Amsterdam.

00:15:48.200 --> 00:15:49.180
And what about this one?

00:15:50.170 --> 00:15:51.130
That's...!

00:15:52.810 --> 00:15:55.210
She's very pretty.

00:15:58.580 --> 00:15:59.800
You opened my drawer?!

00:16:00.120 --> 00:16:01.050
You were hiding it.

00:16:01.250 --> 00:16:03.340
You have your arm
around her!

00:16:08.390 --> 00:16:09.680
This is...

00:16:10.560 --> 00:16:13.620
All right, explain yourself
to the manager!

00:16:14.600 --> 00:16:17.960
Actually, I used to live
with her.

00:16:24.240 --> 00:16:24.930
She's my younger sister.

00:16:33.250 --> 00:16:34.140
Surprised?

00:16:35.990 --> 00:16:36.820
He's sharp...

00:16:37.320 --> 00:16:39.610
There's nothing to prove
that she's your sister.

00:16:39.990 --> 00:16:42.320
Really? People say we
look alike.

00:16:42.560 --> 00:16:43.680
Now that you mention it...

00:16:43.830 --> 00:16:44.790
Her teeth sparkle, too.

00:16:45.090 --> 00:16:46.920
Looking at all these
things made me hungry.

00:16:47.000 --> 00:16:48.190
Let's fix dinner.

00:16:48.330 --> 00:16:49.820
You have so many ingredients.

00:16:50.170 --> 00:16:52.030
You opened my
refrigerator, too?!

00:17:00.480 --> 00:17:01.970
You're good, Grandma.

00:17:02.750 --> 00:17:06.150
Have a seat, Grandma. We
can manage by ourselves.

00:17:06.580 --> 00:17:09.540
Don't disparage your elders.

00:17:12.960 --> 00:17:14.510
Where's the pepper?

00:17:14.820 --> 00:17:15.780
Right here.

00:17:17.660 --> 00:17:18.280
Forgive me...

00:17:18.990 --> 00:17:19.880
That's all right.

00:17:34.180 --> 00:17:35.730
You have a very
convenient kitchen.

00:17:36.180 --> 00:17:38.740
It's designed for
my future wife.

00:17:43.590 --> 00:17:44.850
Say, Godai!

00:17:45.250 --> 00:17:45.970
Yes!

00:17:46.320 --> 00:17:49.220
Would you mind picking up a
bottle of Wocestershire sauce?

00:17:49.390 --> 00:17:50.510
Me?

00:17:51.560 --> 00:17:52.420
We're all out.

00:17:52.590 --> 00:17:55.610
You're not doing anything,
right? Go get it for us.

00:17:56.130 --> 00:17:57.720
We appreciate it, Godai.

00:18:06.110 --> 00:18:07.700
What am I doing, anyway?

00:18:31.170 --> 00:18:33.730
Grandma! What're you
doing out here?

00:18:34.640 --> 00:18:35.620
Thanks for getting that.

00:18:36.000 --> 00:18:36.480
Where are they?

00:18:36.570 --> 00:18:37.460
Upstairs.

00:18:46.520 --> 00:18:46.980
Damn!

00:18:58.390 --> 00:19:01.350
If Mitaka lays even a finger
on the manager...

00:19:01.430 --> 00:19:02.550
he's gonna pay!

00:19:04.630 --> 00:19:05.520
Manager!

00:19:12.610 --> 00:19:13.200
Yes?

00:19:14.240 --> 00:19:15.360
Manager!

00:19:15.840 --> 00:19:17.360
Is something the matter?

00:19:18.080 --> 00:19:20.480
Grandma! Where were you?

00:19:20.880 --> 00:19:23.000
I went to meet Yusaku.

00:19:23.620 --> 00:19:26.580
That's a relief. We didn't
know where you went.

00:19:26.690 --> 00:19:28.680
Sorry...sorry.

00:19:33.630 --> 00:19:34.790
She's back...

00:19:34.900 --> 00:19:36.230
Yes, just a moment ago.

00:19:37.100 --> 00:19:39.220
You mustn't worry us
like that!

00:20:01.660 --> 00:20:02.520
Cheers!

00:20:06.130 --> 00:20:08.820
Your cooking is always
so delicious, Mr. Mitaka.

00:20:08.930 --> 00:20:11.120
It's because you helped,
Ms. Otonashi.

00:20:12.170 --> 00:20:13.390
Delicious!

00:20:13.500 --> 00:20:16.020
It's called beef stroganoff,
Grandma.

00:20:34.960 --> 00:20:39.190
Free drinks, free food.
I had a wonderful time today.

00:20:39.360 --> 00:20:40.820
Didn't we, Manager?

00:20:41.060 --> 00:20:41.580
Yes...

00:21:12.860 --> 00:21:15.120
Was his money enough
to make you give up?

00:21:16.230 --> 00:21:17.020
Grandma...

00:21:18.900 --> 00:21:20.730
Who said I'm giving up?!

00:21:24.940 --> 00:21:27.670
You're exactly like
your grandpa.

00:21:30.380 --> 00:21:36.370
There was another, very rich
man who wanted to marry me.

00:21:36.650 --> 00:21:37.700
You're making that up.

00:21:42.890 --> 00:21:47.580
He was so handsome
just like Coach Mitaka.

00:21:48.130 --> 00:21:52.720
Your grandpa was just like
you. Wishy-washy.

00:21:53.040 --> 00:21:56.870
Why do you think I chose your
grandpa over that hunk?

00:21:59.540 --> 00:22:04.060
It's because he had that
helpless look in his eyes...

00:22:04.150 --> 00:22:08.310
that told me he'd love me
until the day he died.

00:22:08.720 --> 00:22:15.310
Love, not money, makes
a woman happiest.

00:22:16.590 --> 00:22:17.520
Grandma...

00:22:29.300 --> 00:22:32.230
Now I understand why she
brought me to Mitaka's place.

00:22:35.410 --> 00:22:37.970
But I regret it now!

00:22:39.980 --> 00:22:42.310
It was a moment of
poor judgement!

00:22:42.480 --> 00:22:46.970
If they both loved me equally, I
shouldn've gone for the money!

00:22:47.590 --> 00:22:49.780
Grandma! Whose side
are you on?!

00:22:52.460 --> 00:22:54.510
Ready to give up?

00:22:54.900 --> 00:22:55.860
Godai...

00:22:56.930 --> 00:23:00.830
What happened? This time,
both of you disappeared.

00:23:01.340 --> 00:23:03.130
You had me worried.

00:23:04.010 --> 00:23:04.770
Sorry...

00:23:04.840 --> 00:23:07.930
Manager, he says he's
ready to give up.

00:23:08.610 --> 00:23:09.700
Give up what?

00:23:10.480 --> 00:23:11.570
I haven't given up!

00:23:12.810 --> 00:23:14.970
Don't tell me, tell
the manager.

00:23:15.620 --> 00:23:17.080
What're you giving up?

00:23:24.830 --> 00:23:25.690
Well, that's...

00:23:29.030 --> 00:23:30.720
So wishy-washy!

00:23:35.770 --> 00:23:38.790
Guess I'll just have to
stay a while longer!

00:23:49.920 --> 00:23:53.320
Grandma Yukari sets up
a date for Godai and me.

00:23:53.660 --> 00:23:56.390
Will it go according
to her plans?

00:23:56.830 --> 00:24:01.460
Next: "The Great Date Race!
Kyoko and Godai Have Left the Building!"

00:24:01.860 --> 00:24:04.850
Is it just me...
Or do I smell a plot?
